   "subject": "Phylogenetic tree at individual level",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello,<br>I am new to DartR and have been playing around with the tutorials (<a href=\"http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787726000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1yjSRGAxexuWilakTCyt6j\">http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR</a>). Is there a way to create a phylogenetic tree at the individual level instead of the population level?<br><br>gl &lt;- <a href=\"http://testset.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://testset.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787726000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1lOzmeVMiVbw5dhl9bPLjW\">testset.gl</a><br>nInd(gl) # 250 individuals<br>nPop(gl) # 30 populations<br>gl.tree.nj(gl) #  display genetic similarity between populations in the form of a phenetic tree <br><br>In this example, I would like to create a phylogenetic tree of individuals (n = 250), not populations (n = 30)<br><br>Kind regards,<br>Nicholas<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "_b5sB6SZAAAJ",
   "from": "Jose Luis Mijangos",
   "author": "592079bda2cb3220",
   "date": "2024-09-16T06:46:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: Phylogenetic tree at individual level",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Nicholas,<div><br></div><div>You can use a genetic distance matrix between individuals as input, see below:</div><div><br></div><div>library(dartRverse)<br>gl &lt;- <a href=\"http://testset.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://testset.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787727000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XiyZHWKabi6J5qAmfkt34\">testset.gl</a><br>mdis &lt;- gl.dist.ind(gl)<br>gl.tree.nj(gl, dist.matrix = mdis)</div><div><br></div><div>Note that genetic distance and phylogenetic distance are not the same thing, have a look at the link below:<br><br></div><div><a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/share/66e7d350-cce0-8004-b4b3-dd37721b9c0b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://chatgpt.com/share/66e7d350-cce0-8004-b4b3-dd37721b9c0b&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787727000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2lTe_3N3bs9xltklR4VvLj\">https://chatgpt.com/share/66e7d350-cce0-8004-b4b3-dd37721b9c0b</a></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Luis  <br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Monday 16 September 2024 at 1:11:31 pm UTC+10 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nichola...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hello,<br>I am new to DartR and have been playing around with the tutorials (<a href=\"http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787727000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1CpOCGZoaRBc6ik6rkKL6Z\">http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR</a>). Is there a way to create a phylogenetic tree at the individual level instead of the population level?<br><br>gl &lt;- <a href=\"http://testset.gl\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://testset.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787727000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XiyZHWKabi6J5qAmfkt34\">testset.gl</a><br>nInd(gl) # 250 individuals<br>nPop(gl) # 30 populations<br>gl.tree.nj(gl) #  display genetic similarity between populations in the form of a phenetic tree <br><br>In this example, I would like to create a phylogenetic tree of individuals (n = 250), not populations (n = 30)<br><br>Kind regards,<br>Nicholas<br></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
