     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Hi Nicholas,<div><br></div><div>I would recommend exporting your genlight as a fasta file, and then running it in IQtree using the ascertainment bias correction for SNPs. This will give you a publishable phylogenetic tree with individual tips.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"display:block\"><div style=\"display:inline-block\" role=\"link\"><a style=\"border-radius:10px;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;display:block;width:300px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models#ascertainment-bias-correction\" dir=\"ltr\" role=\"button\" width=\"300\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models%23ascertainment-bias-correction&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dbwfGIpB3xxawWyBfZUs4\"><table style=\"table-layout:fixed;border-collapse:collapse;width:300px;background-color:rgb(229,230,233);font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"300\"><tbody><tr><td><table bgcolor=\"#E5E6E9\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"300\" style=\"font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;table-layout:fixed;background-color:rgb(229,230,233)\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 0px\"><div style=\"max-width:100%;margin:0px 16px;overflow:hidden\"><div style=\"font-weight:500;font-size:12px;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;text-align:left\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models#ascertainment-bias-correction\" style=\"text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models%23ascertainment-bias-correction&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dbwfGIpB3xxawWyBfZUs4\"><font color=\"#272727\" style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.847)\">Substitution Models</font></a></div><div style=\"font-weight:400;font-size:11px;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;text-align:left\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models#ascertainment-bias-correction\" style=\"text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models%23ascertainment-bias-correction&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dbwfGIpB3xxawWyBfZUs4\"><font color=\"#808080\" style=\"color:rgba(0,0,0,0.498)\">iqtree.org</font></a></div></div></td><td style=\"padding:0px 12px 0px 0px\" width=\"36\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models#ascertainment-bias-correction\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.iqtree.org/doc/Substitution-Models%23ascertainment-bias-correction&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dbwfGIpB3xxawWyBfZUs4\"><img style=\"display:inline-block;width:36px;min-height:36px\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\"></a></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></a></div></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>Renee</div><div><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 16 Sep 2024, at 11:11 AM, Nicholas Wu &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nichola...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br><div>Hello,<br>I am new to DartR and have been playing around with the tutorials (<a href=\"http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DuxvKziIeyJCVczM3cj_w\">http://georges.biomatix.org/dartR</a>). Is there a way to create a phylogenetic tree at the individual level instead of the population level?<br><br>gl &lt;- <a href=\"http://testset.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://testset.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0L6wiR64qs6reUWCPeN06p\">testset.gl</a><br>nInd(gl) # 250 individuals<br>nPop(gl) # 30 populations<br>gl.tree.nj(gl) #  display genetic similarity between populations in the form of a phenetic tree <br><br>In this example, I would like to create a phylogenetic tree of individuals (n = 250), not populations (n = 30)<br><br>Kind regards,<br>Nicholas<br><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;dartR&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dartr+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/dartr/454c976b-5b6f-4a74-98c3-39e5c268eb24n%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/dartr/454c976b-5b6f-4a74-98c3-39e5c268eb24n%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792457787732000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2X2F32GO0kKqqo96vFQajV\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/dartr/454c976b-5b6f-4a74-98c3-39e5c268eb24n%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\n</div></blockquote></div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;dartR&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dartr+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></blockquote></div>"
