  {
   "id": "TASGxy6GAgAJ",
   "from": "Peter Unmack",
   "author": "d87216285ace7535",
   "date": "2024-09-22T01:31:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: [dartR] Phylogenetic tree at individual level",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I make a column in my metadata file called phylo_label that I want to \r<br>use as the label for each individual.  Then I apply the following commands.\r<br>\r<br>pop(gl)&lt;- rep(&quot;&quot;,nInd(gl))\r<br>indNames(gl)&lt;- gl@other$ind.metrics$phylo_label\r<br>gl2fasta(gl, method=3, outfile=&quot;fasta_file.fas&quot;, outpath=getwd())\r<br>\r<br>View the help file for gl2fasta to better understand the full range of \r<br>the options for this command.  Method 3 only exports the variable base \r<br>for each snp and is generally sufficient for most analyses.\r<br>\r<br>Cheers\r<br>Peter\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On 20/09/2024 11:21 am, Hewan Demissie wrote:\r<br>&gt; Would you advise us on how to export the dart file to the Fasta file?\r<br>&gt; ------------------------------------------------\r<br>&gt; Hewan Demissie\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Tue, Sep 17, 2024 at 5:20 AM Renee Catullo &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">renee....@gmail.com</a> \r<br>&gt; &lt;mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">renee....@gmail.com</a>&gt;&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;     Hi Nicholas,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;     I would recommend exporting your genlight as a fasta file, and then\r<br>&gt;     running it in IQtree using the ascertainment bias correction for\r<br>&gt;     SNPs. This will give you a publishable phylogenetic tree with\r<br>&gt;     individual tips.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
